    "title": "Saw mill fire in Cayuga County prompts multi-agency response - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CAYUGA COUNTY, N.Y. (WSYR-TV) — Reports of a fire at a saw mill in the Town of Ira prompted numerous agencies to respond on Wednesday, July 30. Flames and explosions were reported to 911 dispatchers in the 2400 block of Ira Station Road just before 5:30 p.m. At least 10 fire departments were called in to help. It is unknown at this time what caused the fire or if any injuries were reported. This story is developing and NewsChannel 9 will update you when we receive new information. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSYR.",
